  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Agricultural Production in SKS- SP FSL.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtSamaritan&#x2019;s Purse proposes to improve agricultural production through the capacity building of farmers using the Training of Trainers (ToT) approach and distribution of&#xa0; 55.25 MT of open pollinated varieties (OPVs) of sorghum and sesame seed using the voucher modality to 5,000 households (HHs) (4,000 HHs from Western Jebel and 1,000 from the Central Region).&#xa0; In addition, 2.25 MT of assorted vegetable seed will be provided to 5,000 targeted HHs (4,000 in Western Jebel, 1,000 in the Central Region) through the in-kind modality for improved nutrition and to assist in bridging the hunger gap before the harvest of the main staple crop.lt/pgtltpgt&#xa0; ltbrgtThe intervention will also provide 10,000 malodas to aid in land preuy7jhparation and weeding, as well as watering cans for complementary irrigation of vegetable gardens. Furthermore, the program will support 500 HHs (part of the 5,000 HHs mentioned above) with tractor plowing using the voucher modality, through commercial service providers. These will plow and plant 2,000 feddans. The program will target 80% internally displaced person (IDP) HHs and 20% host community HHs in both locations (Central Region and Western Jebel).lt/pgtltpgtltbrgtThe selection of target groups for the agricultural support program in Yabus Payam will prioritize IDPs, vulnerable HHs, and those with demonstrated farming capacity. Beneficiaries will include women-headed HHs, persons with disabilities (PWDs), and elderly individuals with limited access to agricultural inputs. Households must show willingness and capacity to farm (able-bodied person), with access to land provided through the Secretariat of Agriculture (SoA) or other arrangements, and commit to utilizing inputs for the intended purpose. Selection will be guided by vulnerability criteria, community endorsement, and adherence to program guidelines to ensure inclusivity and equitable resource distribution.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
